WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:26.950
The Ghosts of Eddington Castle

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:35.950
on the border of England and Scotland. The year is 1605.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.950
Halt! Who goes there?

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.950
Let us in. We have a prisoner.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:40.950
Who is this man?

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.950
Robert Mackenzie. He's a traitor. He has to be hanged.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.950
Place him in the dungeon. Take him to the dungeon.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.950
Get up, Mackenzie.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.950
Take your hands off me, you English pig!

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.950
Why you?

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:04.950
Put your sword away. He will be hanged as every traitor should be, and then his body will be thrown from the castle walls.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.950
Take him to the dungeon.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.950
Put him in there.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:21.950
The following night, the night before Robert Mackenzie was due to be hanged,

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.950
a hay wagon arrived at the gates of the castle.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.950
Halt! Who goes there?

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:31.950
Gabriel West. What is your business here?

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.950
You know me. I bring hay for your horses.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:37.950
Wait. Let me look.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.950
Can I go in now?

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:40.950
You may pass.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:44.950
Thank you. Get up!

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.950
Whoa!

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.950
Yes, stupid Mack. Stand still.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.950
Wait a minute.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000
Who's that?

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.950
Don't say a word.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.950
Who are you? And how did you get into my wagon?

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:05.950
Don't ask questions.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.950
I will call for help.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.950
If you do anything, I will kill you.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.950
No, stop. What do you want from me?

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.950
Tell me where the dungeons are.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.950
You don't know where the dungeons are.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.950
Can you feel the blade of my knife on your throat?

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:23.950
Alright.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.950
I will kill you if you don't do as I say.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:27.950
Stop.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.950
Where are the dungeons?

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.950
On the other side of this courtyard.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.950
Right.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:38.950
Now listen to me. Unload your hay and wait here.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.950
I will be back in five minutes.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.950
I intend to leave the castle in your wagon.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:45.950
I should I wait for you.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.950
Because if you don't, I will kill you.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.950
And what is to stop me leaving the castle without you?

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:53.950
Before you come back.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.950
I have friends outside the castle waiting for this wagon.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.950
If I am not on it, they will kill you.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.950
I will do as you ask.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.950
But why do you want to go to the dungeons?

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.950
My husband is there.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.950
Your husband?

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.950
The traitor Robert Mackenzie is your husband.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.950
Don't dare use the word traitor in front of me again.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.950
Don't tell me again.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:19.950
Where are the dungeons?

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.950
Across the courtyard and then down some steps.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:23.950
Thank you.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:24.950
But you'll never get there.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:25.950
Why not?

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.950
There is a guard at the top of the steps and another at the bottom.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.950
There will not be a problem.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.950
Just make sure you are ready to leave when I return.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:39.950
And if you breathe a word to these guards, you will die an ugly death when you leave this castle.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.000
I understand.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.950
I am not waiting for you.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:47.000
You dangerous witch.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:49.950
Guard.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:50.950
Who is there?

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.950
It is me.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:53.950
Who?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:54.950
Who is it?

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.950
Come closer.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.000
Who are you and what?

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.950
Who goes there?

00:04:09.000 --> 00:04:11.000
Adam is it you?

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.000
What is going on?

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.950
Who is there?

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:23.950
Is it time?

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.950
Robert, it is me.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:27.950
Elizabeth?

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:28.950
Yes.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:29.950
Oh my God.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:30.950
Let me hold you.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.950
Robert, quickly we must leave.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:35.950
Leave.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:36.950
Yes, come.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:37.950
My God.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.950
What have you done?

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:40.950
Have you killed the guard?

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.950
I have killed two guards.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.950
I will kill as many as it takes to free you.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:46.950
Now come.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.950
But how can we escape?

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:49.950
What are we to do?

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.950
Robert, there is no time to talk.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.000
Put on this cloak and follow me.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.950
You see the wagon on the other side of the courtyard.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:05.950
Yes.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.950
We are going to escape in that.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.000
Come on.

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.000
Get up.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.950
What the?

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.950
The stupid fool.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.950
The wagon has gone.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:23.950
What's happening?

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:24.950
Quick.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:26.950
There are horses over there.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.000
We can still get out before they lower the gate.

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:31.950
Stop.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:32.950
Who are you?

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.950
We need two horses.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:35.950
What?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:36.950
Oh.

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:38.000
Quickly.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:42.950
That was the gate.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.000
The prisoner is escaping.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:48.950
God.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:49.950
Yes, Captain?

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:50.950
Give me your crossbow.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:51.950
Yes, Captain.

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.000
What are you?

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:56.950
Robert.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:57.950
Elizabeth.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.950
I've been hit.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.950
Robert, don't stop.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.950
I've been hit.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:04.950
I'm dying.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.000
Wait.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:10.000
Hold on to me.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.000
We can ride on one horse.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.950
Elizabeth, save yourself.

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.950
Leave me to die here.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.950
Why are you so spineless, Robert?

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.000
Hold on to me.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.000
Then horses ask for them.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.950
Leave me, Elizabeth.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:45.950
Hold on to me, Robert.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:51.950
If we get beyond the village, we'll be in the forest and there will never catch us.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:53.950
I can't go on.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.950
I'm bleeding to death.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:57.950
Wait.

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.950
There's house over there.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.950
We can get there before the English scum come over the hill.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.950
We will ask the people in the house to shelter us.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.950
And if they don't.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.000
If they are true Scots, they will help us.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.000
Robert, let me help you.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.000
Lean against the wall.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:25.950
Go, Princess.

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:26.950
Go.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.000
Run into the forest.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.000
Who's there?

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:38.950
Open the door.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:39.950
Who are you?

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.000
Open the door, I tell you.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.950
Who are you?

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:46.950
And who is this man?

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:47.950
What's happened to him?

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:48.950
Let us in.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:49.950
Why?

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.950
The English are coming after us.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.950
Why are they after you? What have you done?

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.950
You were prisoners, aren't you?

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.950
You must have escaped from Eddington Castle.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.000
I won't let you and they will kill me.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:06.950
There we are.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.000
Fire!

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:12.000
Dear God in heaven, you are not coming in here.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:16.000
Oh my God.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:22.000
You will regret this moment until your dying day.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:31.000
In the name of Scotland, I put a curse on your family for all time.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:33.000
Fire!

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.000
Good.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:39.950
They're both dead.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.950
Oh, God, preserve us.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:42.950
What is your name?

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.950
Andrew McPherson.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:45.950
You're a Scotsman.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.000
Yes, I have.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.950
This dead man is the traitor, Robert Mackenzie.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.000
Mackenzie?

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:54.950
Why are you giving shelter to traitors?

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:57.950
No, no, I'm not giving them shelter. I promise.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.950
People who shelter traitors are also traitors.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:04.950
But I didn't shelter them. I wouldn't let them in.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:05.950
Guards?

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.000
Take him away.

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:08.950
Whoop!

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.950
I have done nothing wrong.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.950
What is the name of this cottage?

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.950
It is known as McPherson's farm.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:17.000
Burn it to the ground.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:36.950
Scotland.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:37.950
2005.

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:38.950
Excuse me.

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:39.950
Yes?

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.950
Are you Walter McPherson?

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:43.950
Yes, I am.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:44.950
Oh!

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:45.950
How amazing!

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:46.950
Sorry?

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:49.950
Well, I've just finished reading your book.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:50.950
Oh.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:51.950
Oh.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:52.950
Oh.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:53.950
Oh.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:54.950
Oh.

00:09:55.000 --> 00:09:55.950
Oh.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:56.950
Oh.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:57.950
Oh.

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:58.950
Oh.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:09:59.950
Oh.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:00.950
Oh.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:01.950
Oh.

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:02.950
Oh.

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.950
Hey, I love you, Jean.

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:06.950
Zhang, it's pretty easy.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.950
Why don't we finish drawing your book?

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:09.950
Which one?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.950
I've written quite a few.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.950
The Ghost of Ed agentan castle.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:15.950
It's brilliant.

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:16.950
Thank you.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.950
My name's Jean Duncan, by the way.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.950
Please am each you miss...

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:22.950
Ms Duncan...

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.950
Oh.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:25.950
Call me Jane.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:26.950
Please am each you Jane.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.950
Tell me.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.950
Really? I'm actually from Eddington.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.450
Are you? Do you live there?

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:39.950
No, I live in Edinburgh. I'm coming home to see my parents.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.500
I see.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.950
Walter, are you English, aren't you?

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.450
Oh, you noticed.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:49.950
I certainly did. I'm surprised.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.950
Surprised? Why?

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:56.950
I thought that the ghosts of Eddington Castle was written by someone from the area.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:01.950
Well, for a start, my ancestors are from the area around Eddington.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:06.450
Right. McPherson is a very common name in the area.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:09.450
And secondly, I own a house in Eddington.

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:12.450
Do you know? Which one?

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.500
McPherson's farmhouse.

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:19.950
You own McPherson's farmhouse?

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:24.450
Yes. Well, I inherited it from my cousin, Alistair.

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:27.450
Oh. Was he?

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:30.450
Was he the man who died there? Yes.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:35.950
Alistair McPherson? Yes, I see. How long?

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.450
It was five years ago.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:40.950
And is it true?

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:42.950
What? Is what true?

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:47.950
Is it true that he only spent one night at the house before he died?

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:52.950
Yes, it is. He died of a heart attack on his first night in the house.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:54.450
Very strange.

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:56.950
I see.

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.950
You know people in the village think...

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.950
I know. I know they think that the farmhouse is haunted.

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:03.950
Yes.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:08.450
Well, I'm not sure. For a start, it isn't the original farmhouse.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:12.450
The original farmhouse burnt down. This one is only 200 years old.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:16.450
I know, but it's built on exactly the same spot.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:16.950
Really?

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:20.450
Really? And take my work for it, Walter.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:25.450
People in Eddington believe that the farmhouse and the castle are haunted.

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:28.450
So many strange things have happened there.

00:12:28.500 --> 00:12:31.450
I know. I spent months researching that book.

00:12:31.500 --> 00:12:35.450
I know all about the horses galloping across the hills near the castle late at night.

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:38.450
Well, a lot of people have heard them.

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:39.450
Have you?

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.450
Well, no.

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:46.450
You see? You actually ask anyone if they've seen these horses and they say,

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:49.450
No, but my uncle McPavish has.

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:55.450
So, I asked if I could meet these uncles and grandfathers and of course they were all dead.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:56.450
Well...

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:01.450
Anyway, I don't care. It's my house and I'm going to live there.

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:05.450
You're going to live at McPherson's farmhouse.

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:06.450
Yes.

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:08.450
What? At the weekends?

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:09.450
No. All the time.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:11.450
Goodness!

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:14.450
Well, you feel safe there.

00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:19.450
Safe? Jane, I've lived in London for the last 20 years.

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:25.450
In my street, every day I see tramps, drug dealers, hooligans, football fans.

00:13:25.500 --> 00:13:27.450
I've had enough.

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:29.450
You've had enough of London?

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:31.450
Absolutely. It's dirty and expensive.

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:35.450
And I'm a writer, not a banker, so I can't afford to live there anymore.

00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:36.450
I see.

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:40.450
And I'm too old for it. Everyone seems to be under 30.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.500
How old are you?

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:44.450
31.

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:47.450
Goodness. I'm 31.

00:13:47.500 --> 00:13:51.450
I was joking, Jane. I'm a little bit older than 31.

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:54.450
Anyway, I decided it was time for a change.

00:13:54.500 --> 00:14:00.450
But... you want to live in McPherson's farmhouse?

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:04.450
No one has lived there for ages. I mean apart from...

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:06.450
Apart from Alistair, I know.

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:08.450
But I am going to live there.

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:12.450
In fact, I moved all my books and a lot of my furniture up there last month.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:15.450
And a nice lady from the village has cleaned the place up for me.

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.450
She's done a wonderful job.

00:14:17.500 --> 00:14:19.450
I'm sure she has.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:22.500
Eddington people are very hardworking.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.450
Tell me something, Walter.

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:27.450
What?

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:31.450
Have you ever spent the night at the farmhouse?

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:33.450
Not yet, no.

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:35.500
Tonight will be the first night.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:43.450
Melrose, next station. Melrose, change here from McGovern, Haven and Eddington.

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.450
We have to change here.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:46.500
Okay.

00:14:57.500 --> 00:14:58.500
Walter.

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:00.450
What?

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:01.450
Wake up.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.450
Why?

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:03.450
We've arrived.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.450
Where are we?

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:05.450
In Eddington.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:06.450
Oh.

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:07.500
Right.

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.450
How are you going to get to the farmhouse?

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:14.450
I don't know.

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:15.450
Like taxi, I suppose.

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:16.450
Taxi!

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:19.450
At this time of night, no chance.

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:20.450
Oh.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:22.450
Well, I'll walk.

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:23.450
Walk?

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:24.450
Don't be silly.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:27.450
It's about three miles outside the village.

00:15:27.500 --> 00:15:30.450
At that case, I don't know what I'll do.

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:34.450
Look, my father will be waiting for me outside the station.

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:36.500
He can give you a lift.

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:54.450
It's awfully nice of you to give me a lift, Mr. Duncan.

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:56.450
Think nothing of it, Mr. McPherson.

00:15:56.500 --> 00:16:00.500
Walter thought you would be able to get a taxi at the station father.

00:16:01.500 --> 00:16:06.450
Well, there is a taxi in the village, but the driver stops work at six o'clock.

00:16:06.500 --> 00:16:09.450
I don't know how I would have done without you.

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:12.450
In London, I go everywhere by bus or taxi.

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:15.450
I don't have a car, waste of time and money.

00:16:15.500 --> 00:16:17.450
What did you see?

00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:20.450
It's a waste of time and money, owning a car.

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:21.450
Really?

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.450
Well, not up here, of course.

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:26.450
I'm sure you need a car all the time up here.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:27.450
Yes.

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.450
I'm sure we do.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.500
We're coming to the farmhouse now.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:45.450
Goodness.

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:46.450
It's dark out here, isn't it?

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:47.450
Yes, it is.

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:48.450
Very dark.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:54.450
I say, Mr. Duncan, could you point your headlights at the front door so I can see what I'm doing?

00:16:54.500 --> 00:16:56.500
Eh, just a minute.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.500
That's marvellous. Thank you.

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:15.450
Well, here we are.

00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.450
Home sweet home.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:19.450
Do you want to come in and have a look around?

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:20.450
Eh.

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:21.450
Come on.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:22.450
Don't be shy.

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:23.450
Jean!

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:24.450
Don't go in there!

00:17:24.500 --> 00:17:25.450
Father!

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:27.450
I mean it!

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:30.450
I don't mind driving, Mr. McPherson, here.

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:33.450
But I don't want you to go into the house.

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:34.450
Sorry, Mr. McPherson.

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:36.450
It's nothing personal.

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:38.450
No, no, I understand.

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:39.450
You country types?

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:41.450
I beg your pardon?

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:42.450
Sorry, I mean...

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:46.450
Walter, Dad and I are going home now.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.450
Here's my phone number.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:51.450
If you need anything, just give me a call.

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:53.450
Well, thank you.

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:55.450
Do you have a phone here?

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:57.450
Ah, no, not yet.

00:17:57.500 --> 00:17:59.450
But I've got a mobile.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:00.450
Here.

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:01.450
The numbers on this card.

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:02.450
Okay.

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:05.450
I'll call you later to make sure everything is alright.

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:06.500
Goodbye.

00:18:08.500 --> 00:18:09.450
Hmm.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:10.450
Thank you, Jane.

00:18:10.500 --> 00:18:12.450
Thanks for everything.

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:13.450
Jean!

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:14.500
Coming!

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:34.450
Good God.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:36.450
It's quiet around here.

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:38.500
And it's so dark.

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:46.500
What on earth is that?

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:51.450
Pull yourself together, Walter.

00:18:51.500 --> 00:18:54.500
It's time to have a look at your new home.

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:58.500
Now where the hell is the light switch?

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:01.450
Don't blast.

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:03.450
The lights aren't working.

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:04.450
Oh, well.

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:06.450
I'll have to sort that out in the morning.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.450
So...

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:11.500
the bedroom's in here, I think.

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:18.450
Jesus Christ, it's a cat.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:20.450
How the hell did you get in here?

00:19:20.500 --> 00:19:22.500
Well, you're going out.

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:25.500
How'd you go?

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:30.450
Oh, my God.

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:32.450
There's that noise again.

00:19:32.500 --> 00:19:33.450
There we are.

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:34.450
Fire!

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:36.450
Walter, pull yourself together.

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:38.500
There are no ghosts at Eddington Castle.

00:19:42.500 --> 00:19:43.500
Time for bed.

00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:46.500
I wish to God there was some whiskey somewhere.

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:51.500
What?

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:53.500
Where am I?

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:55.450
Hello?

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:56.450
Walter?

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:57.450
Who's that?

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:58.450
It's Jane.

00:19:58.500 --> 00:19:59.450
Jane Duncan.

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:01.450
It's Jane.

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:02.450
Oh, Jane.

00:20:02.500 --> 00:20:03.450
Hello.

00:20:03.500 --> 00:20:04.450
What time is it?

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:06.450
It's half past ten.

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:08.450
Sorry, did I wake you up?

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:09.450
No, no.

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:10.500
I was just...

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:13.450
Well, yes, you did actually.

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:15.450
I'm so sorry, Walter.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:17.450
I should have waited until tomorrow.

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:20.500
I just wanted to see if everything was alright.

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:23.450
Yes, everything's fine.

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:27.450
There's no electricity and no whiskey, but apart from that, no problems at all.

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:30.450
Well, I'm very pleased to hear it.

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:33.450
I was wondering what your plans were for tomorrow.

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.500
Well, I hear it.

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.450
My God, what was that?

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:39.450
What?

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:41.450
What is it, Walter?

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:43.450
Someone's knocking on the door.

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:44.450
Fit to wake in the dead.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:45.450
Can't you hear it?

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:47.450
No, Walter.

00:20:47.500 --> 00:20:49.450
I can't hear anything at all.

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:51.450
Open the door.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:53.450
I still might.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:54.450
Did you hear that?

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:55.450
No.

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.450
What's going on?

00:20:57.500 --> 00:21:00.450
There's a woman at the door shouting ahead of.

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:02.450
I'm going to tell her to get lost.

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:04.450
Walter, don't.

00:21:04.500 --> 00:21:06.450
Don't open the door.

00:21:06.500 --> 00:21:08.450
Hold on a second, Jane.

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:09.450
I'll sort it out.

00:21:09.500 --> 00:21:11.450
Walter, stop it.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:13.450
Don't open the door.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:15.450
Open the door.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:17.500
I've just about had enough.

00:21:19.500 --> 00:21:21.450
Open the door.

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:22.450
Who's there?

00:21:22.500 --> 00:21:24.450
Open the door, I tell you.

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:25.450
But who are you?

00:21:25.500 --> 00:21:27.450
Open the door.

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:29.450
They're going to kill us.

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:31.450
Who are you?

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:33.450
My God.

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:34.450
What's happened to this man?

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:36.450
The English are after us.

00:21:36.500 --> 00:21:38.450
The English, what are you talking about?

00:21:38.500 --> 00:21:39.450
Let us in.

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:40.450
No.

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:42.450
Tell me who you are.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:44.450
What the hell?

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.450
Who are all these people?

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:51.450
Oh, my God.

00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:56.450
You will regret this moment until your dying day.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:22:04.450
In the name of Scotland, I put a curse on your family for all time.

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:05.450
Fire!

00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:11.450
Oh, my God.

00:22:11.500 --> 00:22:13.500
It's all true.

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:20.450
Walter, what's happened?

00:22:20.500 --> 00:22:24.450
Walter!

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:25.450
Hello.

00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:27.450
Is that the police?

00:22:27.500 --> 00:22:28.450
Yes, it is.

00:22:28.500 --> 00:22:32.450
My name is Jane Duncan, and I'm calling from Eddington.

00:22:32.500 --> 00:22:33.450
Eddington.

00:22:33.500 --> 00:22:36.450
Now, that's near Haberne, am I right?

00:22:36.500 --> 00:22:37.450
Yes.

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:39.450
You have to send someone.

00:22:39.500 --> 00:22:41.450
Something terrible has happened.

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:42.450
Really?

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:44.450
Now, what would that be?

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:46.450
I think someone may have been murdered.

00:22:46.500 --> 00:22:47.450
Murdered?

00:22:47.500 --> 00:22:48.450
Where?

00:22:48.500 --> 00:22:50.450
McPherson's farmhouse.

00:22:50.500 --> 00:22:57.450
Please get police and an ambulance there as fast as you can.

00:22:57.500 --> 00:22:58.450
Father?

00:22:58.500 --> 00:22:59.450
What is it, Jane?

00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:01.450
We have to go back to the farmhouse right away.

00:23:01.500 --> 00:23:02.450
Why?

00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:03.450
What's happened?

00:23:03.500 --> 00:23:10.450
Walter is in terrible trouble.

00:23:10.500 --> 00:23:11.450
Oh, my God.

00:23:11.500 --> 00:23:14.450
Walter's at the door.

00:23:14.500 --> 00:23:16.450
Walter, are you all right?

00:23:16.500 --> 00:23:17.450
Please, no more.

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:18.450
He's alive.

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:20.450
Father, here's my phone.

00:23:20.500 --> 00:23:22.450
Call the police again.

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:23.450
Hi.

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:26.450
Walter, can you hear me?

00:23:26.500 --> 00:23:27.450
Yes.

00:23:27.500 --> 00:23:29.450
What happened?

00:23:29.500 --> 00:23:31.450
A man and a woman.

00:23:31.500 --> 00:23:32.450
They were trying to get in.

00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:33.450
A man and a woman?

00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:34.450
Yes.

00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:36.450
What did they look like?

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:37.450
I don't know.

00:23:37.500 --> 00:23:38.450
Oh, no.

00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:39.450
God.

00:23:39.500 --> 00:23:41.450
Did it hit me?

00:23:41.500 --> 00:23:43.450
Did what hit you, Walter?

00:23:43.500 --> 00:23:44.450
The arrow.

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:45.450
The arrow.

00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:46.450
Did it hit me?

00:23:46.500 --> 00:23:47.450
No, Walter.

00:23:47.500 --> 00:23:48.450
It didn't hit you.

00:23:48.500 --> 00:23:49.450
Thank God for that.

00:23:49.500 --> 00:23:50.450
Jane.

00:23:50.500 --> 00:23:51.450
What, Father?

00:23:51.500 --> 00:23:53.450
The ambulance is on its way.

00:23:53.500 --> 00:23:54.450
Good.

00:23:54.500 --> 00:23:55.450
Thank you.

00:23:55.500 --> 00:23:56.450
Is he all right?

00:23:56.500 --> 00:23:58.450
Well, he's alive, but he isn't all right.

00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:02.450
I think he's had a heart attack or something, and...

00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:04.450
And?

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:21.450
I think he's seen the ghosts of Elizabeth and Robert Mackenzie.

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:24.450
My name is Detective Sergeant Jackson, and you are...

00:24:24.500 --> 00:24:28.450
My name's Jane Duncan, and this is my father, Donald.

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:29.450
Hello.

00:24:29.500 --> 00:24:30.450
Hello.

00:24:30.500 --> 00:24:31.450
Sorry to keep you both waiting.

00:24:31.500 --> 00:24:32.450
That's all right.

00:24:32.500 --> 00:24:35.450
We just wanted to make sure that the gentleman was on his way to hospital.

00:24:35.500 --> 00:24:36.450
I understand.

00:24:36.500 --> 00:24:38.450
Is he going to be all right?

00:24:38.500 --> 00:24:39.450
I don't know.

00:24:39.500 --> 00:24:41.450
He's had a heart attack.

00:24:41.500 --> 00:24:43.450
The medics did what they could.

00:24:43.500 --> 00:24:44.450
We'll have to wait and see.

00:24:44.500 --> 00:24:45.450
Okay.

00:24:45.500 --> 00:24:49.450
Now, if you don't mind, I need to ask you one or two questions.

00:24:49.500 --> 00:24:50.450
I know it's a bit late.

00:24:50.500 --> 00:24:51.450
That's all right.

00:24:51.500 --> 00:24:52.450
It's not a problem.

00:24:52.500 --> 00:24:53.450
Right.

00:24:53.500 --> 00:24:57.450
Well, first of all, I understand that you found the gentleman.

00:24:57.500 --> 00:24:58.450
Yes.

00:24:58.500 --> 00:25:00.450
Where was he when you found him?

00:25:00.500 --> 00:25:02.450
He was lying in the doorway.

00:25:02.500 --> 00:25:05.450
And did he tell you what had happened to him?

00:25:05.500 --> 00:25:11.450
Not exactly, but I think he saw the ghosts of Eddington Castle.

00:25:11.500 --> 00:25:12.450
He...

00:25:12.500 --> 00:25:13.450
He saw what?

00:25:13.500 --> 00:25:15.450
He saw two ghosts.

00:25:15.500 --> 00:25:16.450
Er...

00:25:16.500 --> 00:25:18.450
I can't write that in my report.

00:25:18.500 --> 00:25:22.450
Mr. Jackson, you aren't from round here, are you?

00:25:22.500 --> 00:25:24.450
No, I'm from Glasgow.

00:25:24.500 --> 00:25:27.450
Did you see your ruined castle when you drove here?

00:25:27.500 --> 00:25:30.450
No, it's dark. I didn't see anything.

00:25:30.500 --> 00:25:34.450
Well, you drove past Eddington Castle.

00:25:34.500 --> 00:25:38.450
Most people around here would tell you that there are ghosts there.

00:25:38.500 --> 00:25:40.450
Ghosts, see?

00:25:40.500 --> 00:25:41.450
Anybody famous?

00:25:41.500 --> 00:25:45.450
Detective, this is no laughing matter.

00:25:45.500 --> 00:25:48.450
The ghosts are two Scottish freedom fighters.

00:25:48.500 --> 00:25:50.450
Elizabeth and Robert Mackenzie.

00:25:50.500 --> 00:25:54.450
They fought against the English in the 17th century.

00:25:54.500 --> 00:25:57.450
They were killed somewhere in these fields.

00:25:57.500 --> 00:26:01.450
People have seen the ghosts of the English soldiers who killed them as well.

00:26:01.500 --> 00:26:02.450
I see.

00:26:02.500 --> 00:26:05.450
Well, let's talk about what happened this evening.

00:26:05.500 --> 00:26:10.450
By the way, what is your relationship with the gentleman?

00:26:10.500 --> 00:26:13.450
I met him on the train from Eddington at this evening.

00:26:13.500 --> 00:26:15.450
We gave him a lift to the farmhouse.

00:26:15.500 --> 00:26:16.450
I see.

00:26:16.500 --> 00:26:19.450
So you were here when he had the heart attack?

00:26:19.500 --> 00:26:20.450
No.

00:26:20.500 --> 00:26:22.450
We brought Mr. McPherson here.

00:26:22.500 --> 00:26:25.450
But my father didn't want to go into the house.

00:26:25.500 --> 00:26:27.450
Really? Why not?

00:26:27.500 --> 00:26:30.450
Everyone in Eddington is frightened of this house.

00:26:30.500 --> 00:26:33.450
No one has lived here for five years.

00:26:33.500 --> 00:26:37.450
Walter, Mr. McPherson, owns the cottage now.

00:26:37.500 --> 00:26:41.450
But tonight was the first night he spent here.

00:26:41.500 --> 00:26:43.450
He tried to spend here.

00:26:43.500 --> 00:26:44.450
Right.

00:26:44.500 --> 00:26:49.450
And the last person who lived here died the first night he was here.

00:26:49.500 --> 00:26:51.450
So, let me get this straight.

00:26:51.500 --> 00:26:57.450
Mr. McPherson is the owner of the cottage, but he's never spent any time here.

00:26:57.500 --> 00:26:58.450
That's right.

00:26:58.500 --> 00:27:03.450
So, you brought Mr. McPherson to the house and then you went home?

00:27:03.500 --> 00:27:04.450
Yes.

00:27:04.500 --> 00:27:06.450
So, why did you come back to the cottage?

00:27:06.500 --> 00:27:08.450
I came because...

00:27:08.500 --> 00:27:09.450
Yes?

00:27:09.500 --> 00:27:13.450
Well, I called Walter to see if he was all right.

00:27:13.500 --> 00:27:14.450
Yes?

00:27:14.500 --> 00:27:17.450
And something happened while we were on the phone.

00:27:17.500 --> 00:27:20.450
He said there was someone at the door.

00:27:20.500 --> 00:27:23.450
He opened the door and started talking to someone.

00:27:23.500 --> 00:27:25.450
Did you hear who he was talking to?

00:27:25.500 --> 00:27:26.450
No.

00:27:26.500 --> 00:27:28.450
I could only hear Walter's voice.

00:27:28.500 --> 00:27:30.450
What did he see?

00:27:30.500 --> 00:27:32.450
He said, he said...

00:27:32.500 --> 00:27:34.450
Who are you?

00:27:34.500 --> 00:27:35.450
My God.

00:27:35.500 --> 00:27:36.450
What's happened to this man?

00:27:36.500 --> 00:27:37.450
The English.

00:27:37.500 --> 00:27:39.450
What are you talking about?

00:27:39.500 --> 00:27:40.450
No.

00:27:40.500 --> 00:27:41.450
Tell me who you are.

00:27:41.500 --> 00:27:42.450
What the hell?

00:27:42.500 --> 00:27:44.450
Who are all these people?

00:27:44.500 --> 00:27:46.450
Oh, my God.

00:27:46.500 --> 00:27:47.450
It's all true.

00:27:47.500 --> 00:27:48.450
It's all true.

00:27:48.500 --> 00:27:49.450
It's all true.

00:27:49.500 --> 00:27:51.500
It's all true.

00:27:53.500 --> 00:27:55.450
Mr. McPherson?

00:27:55.500 --> 00:27:56.450
Mr. McPherson?

00:27:56.500 --> 00:27:58.450
What?

00:27:58.500 --> 00:28:01.450
Oh, nice.

00:28:01.500 --> 00:28:02.450
What time is it?

00:28:02.500 --> 00:28:04.450
It's half past nine.

00:28:04.500 --> 00:28:06.450
Mr. McPherson and you have a visitor.

00:28:06.500 --> 00:28:08.450
Good morning, Walter.

00:28:08.500 --> 00:28:09.450
Jane.

00:28:09.500 --> 00:28:11.450
How good to see you.

00:28:11.500 --> 00:28:13.450
Good to see you too, Walter.

00:28:13.500 --> 00:28:14.450
Oh, great.

00:28:14.500 --> 00:28:15.450
Yes.

00:28:15.500 --> 00:28:16.450
And they're letting me out today.

00:28:16.500 --> 00:28:17.450
I know.

00:28:17.500 --> 00:28:21.450
Walter, I'm sorry I didn't come to see you earlier.

00:28:21.500 --> 00:28:23.450
I had to go back to Edinburgh.

00:28:23.500 --> 00:28:25.450
But I came back as soon as I could.

00:28:25.500 --> 00:28:28.450
It's so good to see you, Jane.

00:28:28.500 --> 00:28:31.450
You know you saved my life, don't you?

00:28:31.500 --> 00:28:32.450
Oh, Walter.

00:28:32.500 --> 00:28:33.450
It was nothing.

00:28:33.500 --> 00:28:34.450
No.

00:28:34.500 --> 00:28:36.450
You're wrong.

00:28:36.500 --> 00:28:38.450
The doctors told me.

00:28:38.500 --> 00:28:41.450
If you hadn't come to the house, I would have died.

00:28:41.500 --> 00:28:45.450
Well, only too glad to help.

00:28:45.500 --> 00:28:47.450
It was terrifying, you know.

00:28:47.500 --> 00:28:50.450
I can imagine.

00:28:50.500 --> 00:28:54.450
This woman, she looked as if she was going to kill me.

00:28:54.500 --> 00:28:55.450
Yes.

00:28:55.500 --> 00:28:58.450
And do you know what the man said?

00:28:58.500 --> 00:29:08.450
He said, in the name of Scotland, I put a curse on your family for all time.

00:29:08.500 --> 00:29:10.500
A curse?

00:29:11.500 --> 00:29:17.450
Your family is cursed because the man in the farmhouse didn't let Robert and Elizabeth into the house.

00:29:17.500 --> 00:29:20.450
Well, it seems that way.

00:29:20.500 --> 00:29:24.450
Walter, this may seem like a ridiculous question, but...

00:29:24.500 --> 00:29:26.450
Go on.

00:29:26.500 --> 00:29:28.450
Are you going to go back to the farmhouse?

00:29:28.500 --> 00:29:29.450
No way.

00:29:29.500 --> 00:29:30.450
Are you sure?

00:29:30.500 --> 00:29:32.450
Absolutely.

00:29:32.500 --> 00:29:38.450
I'm going to put it on the market, and if no one wants to buy it, I'm going to set fire to it.

00:29:38.500 --> 00:29:40.450
I don't think you should do that.

00:29:40.500 --> 00:29:44.450
I think there's something we can do to solve the problem.

00:29:44.500 --> 00:29:45.450
We?

00:29:45.500 --> 00:29:46.450
Yes.

00:29:46.500 --> 00:29:47.450
We.

00:29:47.500 --> 00:29:48.450
I'll help you.

00:29:48.500 --> 00:29:54.450
Walter, you and I are going to spend the night at the farmhouse tonight.

00:29:54.500 --> 00:29:56.450
What?

00:29:56.500 --> 00:29:58.500
No way.

00:30:05.500 --> 00:30:07.450
Thank you very much, Mr. Pearson.

00:30:07.500 --> 00:30:08.450
You're welcome.

00:30:08.500 --> 00:30:09.450
How much is that?

00:30:09.500 --> 00:30:11.450
Oh, nothing, Jean.

00:30:11.500 --> 00:30:12.450
This trip is on the house.

00:30:12.500 --> 00:30:14.500
Oh, thank you.

00:30:23.500 --> 00:30:25.450
I can't believe that I'm doing this.

00:30:25.500 --> 00:30:27.450
Walter, trust me.

00:30:27.500 --> 00:30:29.500
We're doing the right thing.

00:30:30.500 --> 00:30:39.450
Well, are you going to come in this time?

00:30:39.500 --> 00:30:40.450
Of course.

00:30:40.500 --> 00:30:42.450
You won't be able to see anything.

00:30:42.500 --> 00:30:43.450
Yes, I will.

00:30:43.500 --> 00:30:45.450
I brought these.

00:30:45.500 --> 00:30:46.450
Campals.

00:30:46.500 --> 00:30:48.500
Good idea.

00:30:53.500 --> 00:30:57.500
Oh, Walter, it's absolutely beautiful.

00:30:58.500 --> 00:30:59.450
Yes.

00:30:59.500 --> 00:31:00.450
You're right.

00:31:00.500 --> 00:31:01.450
I'd forgotten.

00:31:01.500 --> 00:31:04.450
By the way, what does your father think about you being here?

00:31:04.500 --> 00:31:06.450
He doesn't know.

00:31:06.500 --> 00:31:07.450
He doesn't know?

00:31:07.500 --> 00:31:08.450
No.

00:31:08.500 --> 00:31:09.450
He thinks I'm in Edinburgh.

00:31:09.500 --> 00:31:12.450
I haven't told him that I came back.

00:31:12.500 --> 00:31:14.450
Jean, this is crazy.

00:31:14.500 --> 00:31:16.450
Walter, relax.

00:31:16.500 --> 00:31:21.450
We just have to spend the night here, and then everything will be fine.

00:31:21.500 --> 00:31:23.450
You know there isn't any electricity.

00:31:23.500 --> 00:31:24.450
Yes.

00:31:24.500 --> 00:31:27.450
So I can't even make you a cup of tea.

00:31:27.500 --> 00:31:29.450
But I do have this.

00:31:29.500 --> 00:31:30.450
A bottle of whiskey.

00:31:30.500 --> 00:31:31.450
Do you want some?

00:31:31.500 --> 00:31:32.450
No.

00:31:32.500 --> 00:31:34.450
And you mustn't have any either.

00:31:34.500 --> 00:31:37.450
You had a heart attack less than a week ago.

00:31:37.500 --> 00:31:38.450
I know.

00:31:38.500 --> 00:31:41.450
That's why I want some whiskey.

00:31:41.500 --> 00:31:44.450
So, what do we do now?

00:31:44.500 --> 00:31:46.450
We wait.

00:31:46.500 --> 00:31:50.450
Jean, if you want to sleep, you can have my room.

00:31:50.500 --> 00:31:52.450
I can sleep here in the kitchen.

00:31:52.500 --> 00:31:54.450
Walter, I don't need to...

00:31:54.500 --> 00:31:55.500
Shh.

00:31:58.500 --> 00:31:59.450
Can you hear that?

00:31:59.500 --> 00:32:00.450
Yes.

00:32:00.500 --> 00:32:02.450
Oh, God.

00:32:02.500 --> 00:32:04.450
Can we call the police or something?

00:32:04.500 --> 00:32:06.450
We don't need the police.

00:32:06.500 --> 00:32:08.450
Let me go to the window.

00:32:08.500 --> 00:32:09.450
No.

00:32:09.500 --> 00:32:12.500
Walter, just stay where you are.

00:32:18.500 --> 00:32:20.500
Robert, let me help you.

00:32:21.500 --> 00:32:23.450
Lean against the wall.

00:32:23.500 --> 00:32:25.450
Go, Princess.

00:32:25.500 --> 00:32:26.450
Go.

00:32:26.500 --> 00:32:28.500
Run into the forest.

00:32:35.500 --> 00:32:36.450
Jane.

00:32:36.500 --> 00:32:37.450
Wait.

00:32:37.500 --> 00:32:39.500
Open the door.

00:32:41.500 --> 00:32:43.450
Don't move, Walter.

00:32:43.500 --> 00:32:45.450
Let me deal with this.

00:32:45.500 --> 00:32:46.450
Jane.

00:32:46.500 --> 00:32:47.500
What are you doing?

00:32:48.500 --> 00:32:50.450
I'm going to open the door.

00:32:50.500 --> 00:32:51.450
Jane, don't.

00:32:51.500 --> 00:32:52.450
They'll kill you.

00:32:52.500 --> 00:32:53.450
Walter.

00:32:53.500 --> 00:32:54.450
Trust me.

00:32:54.500 --> 00:32:57.500
Open the door.

00:32:59.500 --> 00:33:00.450
Welcome.

00:33:00.500 --> 00:33:02.450
Come in.

00:33:02.500 --> 00:33:05.450
You are letting us come in?

00:33:05.500 --> 00:33:06.450
Yes.

00:33:06.500 --> 00:33:08.500
Robert, come.

00:33:09.500 --> 00:33:10.450
I can't.

00:33:10.500 --> 00:33:11.450
Come.

00:33:11.500 --> 00:33:12.450
Come inside the house.

00:33:12.500 --> 00:33:13.500
Sorry.

00:33:14.500 --> 00:33:16.450
Oh, thank you.

00:33:16.500 --> 00:33:18.450
We are escaping from the English.

00:33:18.500 --> 00:33:19.450
I know.

00:33:19.500 --> 00:33:21.450
You are welcome here.

00:33:21.500 --> 00:33:23.450
We are friends.

00:33:23.500 --> 00:33:28.450
My husband is dying, but I don't want the English to catch him.

00:33:28.500 --> 00:33:29.450
I...

00:33:29.500 --> 00:33:30.500
Listen.

00:33:34.500 --> 00:33:36.450
They've gone.

00:33:36.500 --> 00:33:39.450
Robert, we are safe.

00:33:39.500 --> 00:33:42.450
Robert, we are safe.

00:33:42.500 --> 00:33:43.450
Safe.

00:33:43.500 --> 00:33:44.450
Safe.

00:33:44.500 --> 00:33:45.450
Safe.

00:33:45.500 --> 00:33:46.450
Safe.

00:33:46.500 --> 00:33:47.450
Safe.

00:33:47.500 --> 00:33:48.450
Safe.

00:33:48.500 --> 00:33:49.500
Safe.

00:33:55.500 --> 00:33:56.450
If disappeared.

00:33:56.500 --> 00:33:58.450
Yes.

00:33:58.500 --> 00:34:01.450
And I don't think they will come again.

00:34:01.500 --> 00:34:03.450
Jane, you...

00:34:03.500 --> 00:34:05.450
You are amazing.

00:34:05.500 --> 00:34:07.450
Thank you, Walter.

00:34:07.500 --> 00:34:09.450
I don't know what to say.

00:34:09.500 --> 00:34:11.450
Don't say anything.

00:34:11.500 --> 00:34:14.450
Welcome to your new home.

00:34:14.500 --> 00:34:18.450
I hope you spend many happy days here.

00:34:18.500 --> 00:34:20.450
I hope so too.

00:34:20.500 --> 00:34:22.450
Oh, my God.

00:34:22.500 --> 00:34:24.450
I really need a whiskey now.

00:34:24.500 --> 00:34:30.450
Walter, whiskey is not a good idea for someone who's just had a heart attack.

00:34:30.500 --> 00:34:37.450
Jane, meeting the ghosts who gave me the heart attack in the first place wasn't such a good idea.

00:34:37.500 --> 00:34:41.450
If I can survive that, I can survive a glass of whiskey.

00:34:41.500 --> 00:34:43.500
Yeah.

00:35:12.500 --> 00:35:15.500
The Darkest Night.

00:35:39.500 --> 00:35:40.500
Sophie.

00:35:41.500 --> 00:35:42.450
You awake?

00:35:42.500 --> 00:35:43.450
Yes.

00:35:43.500 --> 00:35:45.450
Can you look at the map?

00:35:45.500 --> 00:35:46.450
Sorry?

00:35:46.500 --> 00:35:47.450
Sophie, wake up.

00:35:47.500 --> 00:35:48.450
We're nearly there.

00:35:48.500 --> 00:35:49.450
Oh, right.

00:35:49.500 --> 00:35:51.450
Can you look at the map, please?

00:35:51.500 --> 00:35:52.450
What map?

00:35:52.500 --> 00:35:58.450
Sophie, we've just passed a place called Mold, which means that we must be getting near to Plastag.

00:35:58.500 --> 00:35:59.450
Where?

00:35:59.500 --> 00:36:00.450
Plastag.

00:36:00.500 --> 00:36:01.450
The place where we're going to stay.

00:36:01.500 --> 00:36:02.450
We're nearly there.

00:36:02.500 --> 00:36:05.450
So, why do I have to look on the map?

00:36:05.500 --> 00:36:08.450
Because I wrote some instructions on it.

00:36:08.500 --> 00:36:09.450
Sophie, hurry up.

00:36:09.500 --> 00:36:10.450
We may miss the turning.

00:36:10.500 --> 00:36:11.450
Tom, don't be angry with me.

00:36:11.500 --> 00:36:13.450
Well, well, I need your help.

00:36:13.500 --> 00:36:16.450
I can't drive and look at the map at the same time.

00:36:16.500 --> 00:36:17.450
Okay.

00:36:17.500 --> 00:36:18.450
Okay.

00:36:18.500 --> 00:36:19.450
Let me...

00:36:19.500 --> 00:36:20.450
Tom, look out!

00:36:20.500 --> 00:36:21.450
What?

00:36:21.500 --> 00:36:22.450
What is this?

00:36:22.500 --> 00:36:23.450
The girl!

00:36:23.500 --> 00:36:24.450
You're going to hit that girl!

00:36:24.500 --> 00:36:25.450
What girl?

00:36:25.500 --> 00:36:26.450
The girl in the road!

00:36:26.500 --> 00:36:27.450
Look out!

00:36:27.500 --> 00:36:28.450
Sophie, take your hand off the wheel.

00:36:28.500 --> 00:36:29.450
Oh!

00:36:29.500 --> 00:36:30.500
No!

00:36:34.500 --> 00:36:37.450
What the hell was all that about?

00:36:37.500 --> 00:36:39.450
Are you okay?

00:36:39.500 --> 00:36:41.450
I think so.

00:36:41.500 --> 00:36:44.450
But what about the girl?

00:36:44.500 --> 00:36:45.450
Did you hit her?

00:36:45.500 --> 00:36:48.450
What on earth are you talking about?

00:36:48.500 --> 00:36:51.450
Look, Sophie, I've just crashed the car into...

00:36:51.500 --> 00:36:54.450
What the hell is this?

00:36:54.500 --> 00:36:57.450
We've crashed into a great big mound of earth.

00:36:57.500 --> 00:37:01.450
There was a girl crossing the road, didn't you see her?

00:37:01.500 --> 00:37:03.450
No, I didn't see anyone.

00:37:03.500 --> 00:37:05.450
And anyway, look at the car.

00:37:05.500 --> 00:37:07.450
Oh my God, if you hit her, she could be dead.

00:37:07.500 --> 00:37:09.450
I didn't hit anyone.

00:37:09.500 --> 00:37:11.450
There was no one on the road.

00:37:11.500 --> 00:37:13.450
What's the matter with you?

00:37:13.500 --> 00:37:14.450
Were you dreaming?

00:37:14.500 --> 00:37:15.450
No!

00:37:15.500 --> 00:37:17.450
I saw a girl.

00:37:17.500 --> 00:37:19.450
She stepped right in front of the car.

00:37:19.500 --> 00:37:21.450
And she looked straight at me.

00:37:21.500 --> 00:37:23.450
It was as if she wanted to kill herself.

00:37:23.500 --> 00:37:25.450
Well, she nearly killed us.

00:37:25.500 --> 00:37:28.450
Sophie, where are you going?

00:37:28.500 --> 00:37:30.500
I'm going to look for her!

00:37:31.500 --> 00:37:34.450
Oh, please, God, let her be OK.

00:37:34.500 --> 00:37:36.450
Can you see anything?

00:37:36.500 --> 00:37:38.450
No.

00:37:38.500 --> 00:37:40.450
Oh, there's no one here.

00:37:40.500 --> 00:37:42.450
I told you there wasn't anyone.

00:37:42.500 --> 00:37:45.450
Tom, I saw a girl.

00:37:45.500 --> 00:37:48.450
She stepped out into the road in front of the car.

00:37:48.500 --> 00:37:50.450
What did she look like?

00:37:50.500 --> 00:37:52.450
She was young.

00:37:52.500 --> 00:37:54.450
She looked about 14 and...

00:37:54.500 --> 00:37:56.450
And what?

00:37:56.500 --> 00:37:58.450
Well, she looked...

00:37:58.500 --> 00:38:01.450
I don't know. She looked old-fashioned.

00:38:01.500 --> 00:38:04.450
I've never seen anyone who looked like that.

00:38:04.500 --> 00:38:08.450
And she was carrying something, a kind of bag.

00:38:08.500 --> 00:38:10.450
They looked really old.

00:38:10.500 --> 00:38:13.450
Sophie, I don't think you actually saw anyone.

00:38:13.500 --> 00:38:16.450
I think you were still half asleep.

00:38:16.500 --> 00:38:17.450
Maybe.

00:38:17.500 --> 00:38:20.500
Anyway, we have to do something about the car.

00:38:25.500 --> 00:38:27.500
Let's see if I can start it.

00:38:29.500 --> 00:38:30.450
No.

00:38:30.500 --> 00:38:32.500
OK.

00:38:39.500 --> 00:38:42.450
Well, this car isn't going anywhere.

00:38:42.500 --> 00:38:44.450
What did we hit?

00:38:44.500 --> 00:38:47.500
Well, I thought it was just a moment of Earth.

00:38:50.500 --> 00:38:53.450
But it's really solid.

00:38:53.500 --> 00:38:57.500
It's some kind of round wall or something.

00:38:58.500 --> 00:38:59.450
Oh.

00:38:59.500 --> 00:39:01.450
What is it?

00:39:01.500 --> 00:39:03.450
I think it's a well.

00:39:03.500 --> 00:39:06.450
A well? What, like for water?

00:39:06.500 --> 00:39:07.450
Yes.

00:39:07.500 --> 00:39:10.450
Well, it used to be a well. It's...

00:39:10.500 --> 00:39:12.450
It's been filled in.

00:39:12.500 --> 00:39:14.450
Right.

00:39:14.500 --> 00:39:17.450
So, what are we going to do about the car?

00:39:17.500 --> 00:39:20.450
Oh, try to call someone.

00:39:20.500 --> 00:39:22.450
Oh.

00:39:22.500 --> 00:39:23.450
What?

00:39:23.500 --> 00:39:25.450
I can't get a signal.

00:39:25.500 --> 00:39:26.450
Can you?

00:39:26.500 --> 00:39:28.450
Wait a sec.

00:39:28.500 --> 00:39:30.450
No.

00:39:30.500 --> 00:39:32.450
I can't.

00:39:32.500 --> 00:39:34.450
Oh, not surprising, really.

00:39:34.500 --> 00:39:36.450
We're in the middle of nowhere.

00:39:36.500 --> 00:39:37.450
Oh.

00:39:37.500 --> 00:39:38.450
Look.

00:39:38.500 --> 00:39:39.450
What?

00:39:39.500 --> 00:39:40.450
The sign over there.

00:39:40.500 --> 00:39:41.450
Plus tag.

00:39:41.500 --> 00:39:42.450
Plus tag.

00:39:42.500 --> 00:39:43.450
Oh!

00:39:43.500 --> 00:39:45.450
The place where we're going to stay.

00:39:45.500 --> 00:39:46.450
Yes.

00:39:46.500 --> 00:39:47.450
Oh.

00:39:47.500 --> 00:39:49.450
It's two kilometers down that road.

00:39:49.500 --> 00:39:50.450
Two kilometers?

00:39:50.500 --> 00:39:51.450
Oh, no.

00:39:51.500 --> 00:39:52.450
It's not far.

00:39:52.500 --> 00:39:54.450
We can leave the luggage in the car.

00:39:54.500 --> 00:39:56.450
I'm not leaving anything in the car.

00:39:56.500 --> 00:39:58.450
It could get stolen.

00:39:58.500 --> 00:40:00.450
Sophie, what did you just say?

00:40:00.500 --> 00:40:02.450
We're in the middle of nowhere.

00:40:02.500 --> 00:40:04.450
No one is going to steal anything.

00:40:04.500 --> 00:40:07.450
I am not leaving anything in the car.

00:40:07.500 --> 00:40:10.450
Okay.

00:40:10.500 --> 00:40:13.500
Let's unpack and start walking.

00:40:20.500 --> 00:40:21.450
Grandma?

00:40:21.500 --> 00:40:23.450
What is it, Gwyn?

00:40:23.500 --> 00:40:26.450
There are two people walking down the path.

00:40:26.500 --> 00:40:27.450
Who are they?

00:40:27.500 --> 00:40:28.450
I don't know.

00:40:28.500 --> 00:40:30.450
They're not from around here.

00:40:30.500 --> 00:40:32.450
And they've got a lot of luggage.

00:40:32.500 --> 00:40:33.450
Really?

00:40:33.500 --> 00:40:35.450
Strange.

00:40:35.500 --> 00:40:39.450
I'm expecting some people from London, but they're coming by car.

00:40:39.500 --> 00:40:42.450
I wonder who these people are.

00:40:42.500 --> 00:40:43.450
Don't know.

00:40:43.500 --> 00:40:44.450
We'll go on.

00:40:44.500 --> 00:40:45.450
What?

00:40:45.500 --> 00:40:47.450
Go out and help them.

00:40:47.500 --> 00:40:49.500
Oh, okay.

00:40:50.500 --> 00:40:52.450
Nearly there.

00:40:52.500 --> 00:40:54.450
Oh, good.

00:40:54.500 --> 00:40:56.450
My feet are killing me.

00:40:56.500 --> 00:41:00.450
My arms are killing me from carrying all your luggage.

00:41:00.500 --> 00:41:03.450
I can't carry suitcases in these shoes.

00:41:03.500 --> 00:41:04.450
Right.

00:41:04.500 --> 00:41:05.450
Oh, look.

00:41:05.500 --> 00:41:06.450
Someone's coming.

00:41:06.500 --> 00:41:07.450
Hello?

00:41:07.500 --> 00:41:08.450
Hello?

00:41:08.500 --> 00:41:10.450
Have you come to stay at Plastag?

00:41:10.500 --> 00:41:11.450
Yes.

00:41:11.500 --> 00:41:12.450
Here.

00:41:12.500 --> 00:41:14.450
Let me give you a hand with your luggage.

00:41:14.500 --> 00:41:15.450
Thank you very much.

00:41:15.500 --> 00:41:17.450
Flippin' heck.

00:41:17.500 --> 00:41:18.450
This one's heavy.

00:41:18.500 --> 00:41:19.450
I know.

00:41:19.500 --> 00:41:22.450
I'll take this round the back of the house and up to your room.

00:41:22.500 --> 00:41:24.450
You win the bell and my grand will let you in.

00:41:24.500 --> 00:41:25.450
Okay.

00:41:25.500 --> 00:41:26.450
Thank you.

00:41:26.500 --> 00:41:28.450
Goodness.

00:41:28.500 --> 00:41:30.450
Look at this ancient bell.

00:41:30.500 --> 00:41:32.450
I wonder if it works.

00:41:32.500 --> 00:41:33.450
Yes.

00:41:33.500 --> 00:41:35.450
It does.

00:41:35.500 --> 00:41:36.450
Hello?

00:41:36.500 --> 00:41:37.450
Ah.

00:41:37.500 --> 00:41:45.450
You must be Mr. and Mrs. Parks.

00:41:45.500 --> 00:41:46.450
Is that right?

00:41:46.500 --> 00:41:47.450
Yes.

00:41:47.500 --> 00:41:52.450
Well, I'm Tom Parks and this is my partner, Sophie Richardson.

00:41:52.500 --> 00:41:53.450
Hello.

00:41:53.500 --> 00:41:55.450
Are you Mrs. Craven?

00:41:55.500 --> 00:41:57.450
Yes, that's right.

00:41:57.500 --> 00:41:59.450
Welcome to Plastag.

00:41:59.500 --> 00:42:03.450
Um, did you come by bus from mold?

00:42:03.500 --> 00:42:04.450
No.

00:42:04.500 --> 00:42:05.450
No.

00:42:05.500 --> 00:42:06.450
We came by car.

00:42:06.500 --> 00:42:07.450
Oh.

00:42:07.500 --> 00:42:08.450
So...

00:42:08.500 --> 00:42:10.450
We had an accident.

00:42:10.500 --> 00:42:14.450
I'm afraid I crashed into the old well at the corner of the main road.

00:42:14.500 --> 00:42:17.450
You crashed into the old well.

00:42:17.500 --> 00:42:20.450
How did you manage to do that?

00:42:20.500 --> 00:42:21.450
Well, I...

00:42:21.500 --> 00:42:23.450
It's a long story.

00:42:23.500 --> 00:42:26.450
Well, come inside.

00:42:26.500 --> 00:42:30.450
Right.

00:42:30.500 --> 00:42:32.450
This is your room.

00:42:32.500 --> 00:42:34.450
Oh, it's wonderful.

00:42:34.500 --> 00:42:35.450
Yes.

00:42:35.500 --> 00:42:36.450
It's brilliant.

00:42:36.500 --> 00:42:40.450
Mrs. Craven, is there a garage near here?

00:42:40.500 --> 00:42:43.450
Is there someone who can fix my car?

00:42:43.500 --> 00:42:45.450
I've already asked Green to call someone.

00:42:45.500 --> 00:42:46.450
Thank you.

00:42:46.500 --> 00:42:52.450
I hope you don't mind me asking, but how did the accident happen?

00:42:52.500 --> 00:42:54.450
Well, Sophie...

00:42:54.500 --> 00:42:58.450
I thought I saw someone step into the road, Mrs. Craven.

00:42:58.500 --> 00:43:00.450
I thought we were going to hit her.

00:43:00.500 --> 00:43:03.450
Someone stepped into the road.

00:43:03.500 --> 00:43:05.450
I think I was just dreaming.

00:43:05.500 --> 00:43:11.450
But you think you saw someone on the road at the junction with the road to this house?

00:43:11.500 --> 00:43:12.500
Yes.

00:43:13.500 --> 00:43:16.450
Can you describe the person that you saw?

00:43:16.500 --> 00:43:18.450
It was a girl.

00:43:18.500 --> 00:43:21.450
She was about 14.

00:43:21.500 --> 00:43:22.450
A girl?

00:43:22.500 --> 00:43:24.450
I see.

00:43:24.500 --> 00:43:28.450
Did you notice anything else about her?

00:43:28.500 --> 00:43:29.450
Yes.

00:43:29.500 --> 00:43:31.450
She was carrying an old bag.

00:43:31.500 --> 00:43:33.450
But I was half asleep.

00:43:33.500 --> 00:43:35.450
I think I was dreaming.

00:43:35.500 --> 00:43:36.450
Yes.

00:43:36.500 --> 00:43:39.450
Of course you were.

00:43:39.500 --> 00:43:41.500
Ah, here's Green.

00:43:50.500 --> 00:43:54.450
Gran, David Gower from the garage is here to look at the car.

00:43:54.500 --> 00:43:55.450
Great.

00:43:55.500 --> 00:43:58.450
Can you give us the keys and we'll go and see what we can do?

00:43:58.500 --> 00:44:01.450
Yes, of course. Here you are.

00:44:01.500 --> 00:44:03.500
Thanks.

00:44:04.500 --> 00:44:06.500
You know what? I'm hungry.

00:44:07.500 --> 00:44:10.500
Is there anywhere good to eat?

00:44:12.500 --> 00:44:16.450
Here it is. The Trevord Arts. Thank you.

00:44:16.500 --> 00:44:19.450
Good. I'm starving.

00:44:19.500 --> 00:44:21.450
Last three pounds.

00:44:21.500 --> 00:44:25.500
Here you are. Thank you. Enjoy your evening.

00:44:33.500 --> 00:44:34.450
It looks great.

00:44:34.500 --> 00:44:38.450
Yes, but what's the food like? Remember, we're in the middle of nowhere.

00:44:38.500 --> 00:44:40.450
Let's find out.

00:44:40.500 --> 00:44:41.450
Excuse me.

00:44:41.500 --> 00:44:42.450
Hello. Can I help you?

00:44:42.500 --> 00:44:43.450
Can we see a menu?

00:44:43.500 --> 00:44:45.450
It's on the wall.

00:44:45.500 --> 00:44:46.450
Sorry?

00:44:46.500 --> 00:44:51.450
We don't have a menu. The food we do is written on the wall. Over there.

00:44:51.500 --> 00:44:52.450
Oh, right.

00:44:52.500 --> 00:44:54.450
Do you want me to come back?

00:44:54.500 --> 00:44:56.450
No, I think we can order now.

00:44:56.500 --> 00:45:00.450
I think I'll have the steak pie, please.

00:45:00.500 --> 00:45:01.500
So...

00:45:05.500 --> 00:45:11.450
That was the most boring meal I've ever had in my life.

00:45:11.500 --> 00:45:12.450
Well...

00:45:12.500 --> 00:45:14.450
Have you finished?

00:45:14.500 --> 00:45:16.450
Yes, thank you. Was everything all right?

00:45:16.500 --> 00:45:17.450
Wonderful.

00:45:17.500 --> 00:45:18.450
Good.

00:45:18.500 --> 00:45:20.450
Can you tell me something?

00:45:20.500 --> 00:45:21.450
Yes.

00:45:21.500 --> 00:45:22.450
How old is this pub?

00:45:22.500 --> 00:45:24.450
Oh, it's very old.

00:45:24.500 --> 00:45:27.450
The original pub was built in 1500.

00:45:27.500 --> 00:45:28.450
1500?

00:45:28.500 --> 00:45:29.450
That's amazing.

00:45:29.500 --> 00:45:31.450
Well, that building.

00:45:31.500 --> 00:45:36.450
Burned down a long time ago, but this place is about 300 years old.

00:45:36.500 --> 00:45:39.450
And why is it called the Trevor Arms?

00:45:39.500 --> 00:45:43.450
Ah, well, it's named after the Trevor family.

00:45:43.500 --> 00:45:46.450
They used to be the landowners around here.

00:45:46.500 --> 00:45:50.450
They lived in a big house near here called Plasteg.

00:45:50.500 --> 00:45:52.450
Oh, we're staying there?

00:45:52.500 --> 00:45:53.450
Really?

00:45:53.500 --> 00:45:58.450
And is everything... is everything all right there?

00:45:58.500 --> 00:46:01.450
Yes, everything's fine. Why did you ask?

00:46:01.500 --> 00:46:04.450
Nothing. Excuse me.

00:46:04.500 --> 00:46:06.450
What was that about?

00:46:06.500 --> 00:46:08.450
What was what about?

00:46:08.500 --> 00:46:12.450
She seemed surprised that we were staying at Plasteg.

00:46:12.500 --> 00:46:15.450
Did she? She seemed quite okay to me.

00:46:15.500 --> 00:46:17.450
Anyway, shall we go?

00:46:17.500 --> 00:46:18.450
Okay.

00:46:18.500 --> 00:46:19.450
Oh, just...

00:46:19.500 --> 00:46:20.450
Tom?

00:46:20.500 --> 00:46:21.450
What?

00:46:21.500 --> 00:46:22.450
Look!

00:46:22.500 --> 00:46:23.450
What?

00:46:23.500 --> 00:46:24.450
At the window!

00:46:24.500 --> 00:46:25.450
What is it now?

00:46:25.500 --> 00:46:26.450
That girl again!

00:46:26.500 --> 00:46:29.450
Sophie, come back!

00:46:29.500 --> 00:46:31.450
What are you doing?

00:46:31.500 --> 00:46:33.450
I saw that girl again!

00:46:33.500 --> 00:46:34.450
Which girl?

00:46:34.500 --> 00:46:36.450
The girl we nearly ran down in the road.

00:46:36.500 --> 00:46:37.450
She was at the window!

00:46:37.500 --> 00:46:38.450
Where is she now?

00:46:38.500 --> 00:46:39.450
I don't know.

00:46:39.500 --> 00:46:40.450
She disappeared again.

00:46:40.500 --> 00:46:42.450
I think she's in the woods.

00:46:42.500 --> 00:46:44.450
Sophie, come back!

00:46:44.500 --> 00:46:46.450
I've got to find her!

00:46:46.500 --> 00:46:47.450
Stop!

00:46:47.500 --> 00:46:48.450
Sophie!

00:46:48.500 --> 00:46:51.450
I've got to find her!

00:46:51.500 --> 00:46:52.450
Stop!

00:46:52.500 --> 00:46:53.500
Sophie!

00:46:54.500 --> 00:46:55.500
Sophie!

00:47:01.500 --> 00:47:02.450
What the hell is going on?

00:47:02.500 --> 00:47:04.450
I don't know!

00:47:04.500 --> 00:47:05.450
Jesus!

00:47:05.500 --> 00:47:06.450
Tom!

00:47:06.500 --> 00:47:07.450
I'm scared!

00:47:07.500 --> 00:47:08.450
Me too!

00:47:08.500 --> 00:47:09.450
I...

00:47:09.500 --> 00:47:10.450
Tom!

00:47:10.500 --> 00:47:11.450
What?

00:47:11.500 --> 00:47:12.450
Look out!

00:47:12.500 --> 00:47:13.450
Oh God!

00:47:13.500 --> 00:47:15.450
Are you all right?

00:47:15.500 --> 00:47:16.450
No!

00:47:16.500 --> 00:47:17.450
Wait here!

00:47:17.500 --> 00:47:18.450
I'll get help!

00:47:18.500 --> 00:47:20.450
Go away!

00:47:20.500 --> 00:47:21.500
Who's there?

00:47:22.500 --> 00:47:24.450
Go away!

00:47:24.500 --> 00:47:25.450
Tom!

00:47:25.500 --> 00:47:26.450
It's the girl!

00:47:26.500 --> 00:47:27.450
Go away!

00:47:27.500 --> 00:47:30.450
I've never come near me again!

00:47:30.500 --> 00:47:34.450
If you do, something even worse will happen!

00:47:34.500 --> 00:47:37.500
Ahhh!

00:47:39.500 --> 00:47:40.450
Tom?

00:47:40.500 --> 00:47:42.450
Where am I?

00:47:42.500 --> 00:47:44.450
You're in hospital.

00:47:44.500 --> 00:47:45.450
In hospital?

00:47:45.500 --> 00:47:46.450
What?

00:47:46.500 --> 00:47:47.450
Oh!

00:47:47.500 --> 00:47:48.450
Don't try to move!

00:47:48.500 --> 00:47:50.450
What's the matter with me?

00:47:50.500 --> 00:47:54.450
You have a broken shoulder and a broken arm.

00:47:54.500 --> 00:47:56.450
You're lucky to be alive.

00:47:56.500 --> 00:47:58.450
What happened?

00:47:58.500 --> 00:48:00.450
A tree fell on you.

00:48:00.500 --> 00:48:02.450
Yeah.

00:48:02.500 --> 00:48:04.450
I remember now.

00:48:04.500 --> 00:48:07.450
Well, at least it wasn't that girl.

00:48:07.500 --> 00:48:09.450
It was that girl.

00:48:09.500 --> 00:48:11.450
I'm sure she was responsible.

00:48:11.500 --> 00:48:16.500
If you ever come near me again, something even worse will happen!

00:48:17.500 --> 00:48:22.450
When we were in the woods, she was there.

00:48:22.500 --> 00:48:26.450
When the tree fell on you, she was there.

00:48:26.500 --> 00:48:27.450
Sophie, listen.

00:48:27.500 --> 00:48:28.450
No, Tom.

00:48:28.500 --> 00:48:29.450
You listen to me.

00:48:29.500 --> 00:48:33.450
I am not the only one who has seen this girl.

00:48:33.500 --> 00:48:36.450
Everyone around here knows about her.

00:48:36.500 --> 00:48:40.450
That's why the waitress in the pub wanted to know if everything was all right.

00:48:40.500 --> 00:48:41.450
What waitress?

00:48:41.500 --> 00:48:45.450
And terrible things always happen when she appears.

00:48:45.500 --> 00:48:47.450
How do you know all this?

00:48:47.500 --> 00:48:49.450
Mrs. Craven told me.

00:48:49.500 --> 00:48:51.450
She's here.

00:48:51.500 --> 00:48:54.450
And she wants to tell us the whole story.

00:48:54.500 --> 00:48:55.450
Uh-huh.

00:48:55.500 --> 00:48:57.450
Are you ready for this?

00:48:57.500 --> 00:48:59.450
I guess so.

00:48:59.500 --> 00:49:01.500
I'll go and get her.

00:49:08.500 --> 00:49:10.450
Hello, Mrs. Craven.

00:49:10.500 --> 00:49:11.450
Mr. Parks.

00:49:11.500 --> 00:49:13.450
I'm so sorry.

00:49:13.500 --> 00:49:15.450
Don't be silly, Mrs. Craven.

00:49:15.500 --> 00:49:17.450
This isn't your fault.

00:49:17.500 --> 00:49:19.450
Well, maybe it is.

00:49:19.500 --> 00:49:20.450
Why?

00:49:20.500 --> 00:49:22.450
What do you mean?

00:49:22.500 --> 00:49:25.450
I should have warned you about the girl.

00:49:25.500 --> 00:49:28.450
Mrs. Craven, tell Tom what you told me.

00:49:28.500 --> 00:49:36.500
The girl that Sophie saw is someone who lived in my house five hundred years ago.

00:49:37.500 --> 00:49:44.450
The house was built by a man called Sir John Trevo, sometime around fifteen hundred.

00:49:44.500 --> 00:49:50.450
When he died, his brother Edward became the owner of the house.

00:49:50.500 --> 00:49:56.450
Ashes to ashes, dust to dust.

00:49:56.500 --> 00:50:00.500
We commend our dear brother to be heard.

00:50:01.500 --> 00:50:08.450
My Lord Trevo, allow me to express my deepest sympathy.

00:50:08.500 --> 00:50:10.450
Thank you, Squirt Rwellin.

00:50:10.500 --> 00:50:16.450
My Lord, is it true that you and your family will now live at Plasté?

00:50:16.500 --> 00:50:18.450
Correct, Squirt Rwellin.

00:50:18.500 --> 00:50:22.450
And in a few weeks' time, when we have finished mourning my dear brother John,

00:50:22.500 --> 00:50:27.450
we will have a feast and invite people from all over the county.

00:50:27.500 --> 00:50:33.450
And is it also true that your daughter Dorothy is already sixteen?

00:50:33.500 --> 00:50:40.450
She is indeed, in fact, she will be seventeen in just a few months, I see.

00:50:40.500 --> 00:50:45.450
Did you know that my son Alan finds her most desirable?

00:50:45.500 --> 00:50:48.450
I knew of this, Lwellin.

00:50:48.500 --> 00:50:56.500
It occurred to me that we may use the occasion of the feast to announce the betrudal of my son and your daughter.

00:50:57.500 --> 00:50:59.450
This was my idea, too.

00:50:59.500 --> 00:51:00.450
Dorothy?

00:51:00.500 --> 00:51:02.450
Yes, Father.

00:51:02.500 --> 00:51:05.450
I'm going to make an announcement to the servants.

00:51:05.500 --> 00:51:08.450
I would like you to be there when I do it.

00:51:08.500 --> 00:51:09.500
Yes, Father.

00:51:17.500 --> 00:51:19.450
Good morning, everyone.

00:51:19.500 --> 00:51:24.450
I, Edward Trevoire, am now a master of Plasté.

00:51:24.500 --> 00:51:30.450
And I want you to know that life in the great house will continue as before.

00:51:30.500 --> 00:51:34.450
Everyone will continue to do the work they are doing now.

00:51:34.500 --> 00:51:35.450
Oh, God bless you, sir.

00:51:35.500 --> 00:51:36.450
Oh, thank you.

00:51:36.500 --> 00:51:37.450
Thank you.

00:51:37.500 --> 00:51:38.450
Thank you.

00:51:38.500 --> 00:51:39.450
Thank you.

00:51:39.500 --> 00:51:44.450
For now, the house is in mourning for my dear brother.

00:51:44.500 --> 00:51:49.450
Very soon, we will have a great feast of celebration.

00:51:49.500 --> 00:51:57.500
And the cause of celebration will be the announcement of the marriage of my daughter Dorothy to Alan Lwellin.

00:52:05.500 --> 00:52:08.450
Young Miss Dorothy is to marry Alan Lwellin.

00:52:08.500 --> 00:52:10.450
I cannot believe it.

00:52:10.500 --> 00:52:13.500
Alan Lwellin, such a horrible man.

00:52:14.500 --> 00:52:16.450
And did you see the young girl's face?

00:52:16.500 --> 00:52:19.450
She didn't look very happy about the idea.

00:52:19.500 --> 00:52:20.450
You're right.

00:52:20.500 --> 00:52:22.500
She looked shocked.

00:52:29.500 --> 00:52:35.450
So, Dorothy, you are to be married in June on the occasion of your 17th birthday.

00:52:35.500 --> 00:52:39.450
Father, this is not what I expected.

00:52:39.500 --> 00:52:41.450
Not what you expected.

00:52:41.500 --> 00:52:42.450
What do you mean?

00:52:42.500 --> 00:52:45.450
I feel I am not ready for marriage.

00:52:45.500 --> 00:52:47.450
Not ready.

00:52:47.500 --> 00:52:50.450
Dorothy, you're nearly 17.

00:52:50.500 --> 00:52:52.450
Nearly half way through your life.

00:52:52.500 --> 00:52:54.500
Of course you are ready.

00:53:00.500 --> 00:53:04.450
Well, Miss Dorothy, you are to be married.

00:53:04.500 --> 00:53:05.450
Annie, listen.

00:53:05.500 --> 00:53:06.450
Yes, Miss.

00:53:06.500 --> 00:53:08.450
You are the only person I can trust.

00:53:08.500 --> 00:53:10.450
Yes, Miss.

00:53:10.500 --> 00:53:13.450
You know that I do not love Alan Lwellin.

00:53:13.500 --> 00:53:15.450
Oh, Miss Dorothy.

00:53:15.500 --> 00:53:18.450
I am in love with Yvonne Turner.

00:53:18.500 --> 00:53:20.450
Yvonne Turner?

00:53:20.500 --> 00:53:24.450
But Yvonne Turner is just a farm hand.

00:53:24.500 --> 00:53:26.450
And you are a lady.

00:53:26.500 --> 00:53:28.450
Annie, I love him.

00:53:28.500 --> 00:53:30.500
I will not marry Alan Lwellin.

00:53:31.500 --> 00:53:33.450
Yvonne, are you there?

00:53:33.500 --> 00:53:34.450
Yes.

00:53:34.500 --> 00:53:36.450
Yvonne, hold me.

00:53:36.500 --> 00:53:40.450
Yvonne, why are you so cold with me?

00:53:40.500 --> 00:53:43.450
Because you are to marry Alan Lwellin.

00:53:43.500 --> 00:53:47.450
Yvonne, I do not wish to marry Alan Lwellin.

00:53:47.500 --> 00:53:49.450
This is my father's idea.

00:53:49.500 --> 00:53:53.500
It is you who I wish to marry Alan Lwellin.

00:53:54.500 --> 00:53:56.450
Your father is Lord of the manor now.

00:53:56.500 --> 00:53:59.450
He will never allow you to marry someone who works on the land.

00:53:59.500 --> 00:54:01.450
I don't care about my father's wishes.

00:54:01.500 --> 00:54:03.450
I will marry you.

00:54:03.500 --> 00:54:06.450
Dorothy, that is impossible now.

00:54:06.500 --> 00:54:08.450
No, it isn't.

00:54:08.500 --> 00:54:10.450
We will go away from here.

00:54:10.500 --> 00:54:11.450
Go away.

